Certainly! Below is an example of a simple inverter module written in Verilog, which can be used as a top-level module. An inverter takes a single input and produces the logical negation of that input.

### Verilog Code for TopModule Inverter

```verilog
// TopModule Inverter
module TopModule (
    input wire A,      // Input signal
    output wire Y      // Output signal (inverted)
);

// Inverter logic
assign Y = ~A; //

